-- title:
--   Original Lévy stopped nonlinear Taylor L2 energy tails vanish uniformly under changing predictable discounts and adaptive marked cutoffs
-- statement:
--   On the original stopped spectrally negative Lévy source and finite predictable μ, a sequence of path-adaptive jointly predictable marked truncations decreasing to empty has vanishing quadratic C2 Taylor kernel energy even when the predictable discount changes at each truncation n, provided each discount is between zero and one. Dominating by the proved undiscounted adaptive L2 tail bounds every n; an ENNReal squeeze proves convergence. This supplies a moving-weight approximation theorem for original source jump L2 martingale construction without asserting a replacement Poisson law or source compensator.
-- source:
--   W7-07 uniform moving predictable discount L2 source truncation, from proved adaptive L2 8d0d4823 via pointwise quadratic contraction and ENNReal sandwich.

